      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Shortening the hospitalization period during an acute coronary syndrome can lead to a trivialization of the event, and especially causes many questions among patients about their future lifestyle. A secondary medical care in rehabilitation centers allows to combine the numerous benefits of physical training and to answer to their questioning, through to both a collective and individual therapeutic education."},
